 how='Your eyes make tears all day long, even when you are happy. These "basal" tears keep the surface of your eyes wet, smooth and protected. "Reflex" tears flood in when something irritates your eyes, like smoke, dust or onions. "Emotional" tears come when you feel sad, happy or moved. Crying is linked to your nervous system: after a good cry, many people feel calmer, which may be your body switching from stress mode to rest mode.',
